BT 1 0 0 1 0 103.8 Tm /F1 9.8 Tf 14.2 TL (The first implementation derived circulation from a constant-strength vortex-panel linear system whose) Tj T* (boundary condition was zero normal velocity at collocation points. Releasing the TE Kutta condition in) Tj T* (several arrangements \(extra row, replacing the TE row, sources + one global circulation vortex at the TE) Tj T* -0.071445 Tw (then at the quarter chord, ridge/Tikhonov regularisation\) never converged: residuals ~193 and absurd Cl \(48\)) Tj T* 0 Tw (or negative Cl for cambered airfoils \(-10.2 on s1223\), plus a flat plate that still carried Cl 4.3 at zero angle.) Tj T* (The normal-BC matrix is near-singular for multi-element stacks, TE-adjacent panels swamp the Kutta) Tj T* (sensitivity, and sign extraction of Q = u - i v was a constant source of error. The pragmatic answer: keep) Tj T* (JavaFoil as the authority and drive the field with the circulation it already produces. See chapter 7.) Tj T* ET
